  "id": "warrington-recognition-memory-test",
  "term": "Warrington Recognition Memory Test",
  "definition": "The Warrington Recognition Memory Test is a memory test that includes word and face recognition tasks. In research on temporal lobe epilepsy, its Faces section is commonly used to assess visual or facial memory, and poorer scores have been linked especially to right anterior temporal lobectomy.",
